00:04:38,571 --> 00:04:44,571
Unleash the power behind the armor.

2
00:09:17,142 --> 00:09:23,142
Iron Man 3 is a action, adventure, science fiction film directed by Shane Black.

3
00:13:55,714 --> 00:14:01,714
When Tony Stark's world is torn apart by a formidable terrorist called the
Mandarin, he starts an odyssey of rebuilding and retribution.

4
00:18:34,285 --> 00:18:40,285
Tony Stark, played by Robert Downey Jr..

5
00:23:12,857 --> 00:23:18,857
Pepper Potts, played by Gwyneth Paltrow.

6
00:27:51,428 --> 00:27:57,428
Colonel James Rhodes, played by Don Cheadle.

7
00:32:30,000 --> 00:32:36,000
Aldrich Killian, played by Guy Pearce.

8
00:37:08,571 --> 00:37:14,571
Maya Hansen, played by Rebecca Hall.

9
00:41:47,142 --> 00:41:53,142
Happy Hogan, played by Jon Favreau.

10
00:46:25,714 --> 00:46:31,714
Iron Man 3 is a 2013 American superhero film based on the Marvel Comics character Iron Man,
produced by Marvel Studios and distributed by Walt Disney Studios Motion Pictures.

11
00:51:04,285 --> 00:51:10,285
It is the sequel to Iron Man (2008) and Iron Man 2 (2010), and the
seventh film in the Marvel Cinematic Universe (MCU).

12
00:55:42,857 --> 00:55:48,857
The film was directed by Shane Black from a screenplay he
co-wrote with Drew Pearce, and stars Robert Downey Jr.

13
01:00:21,428 --> 01:00:27,428
as Tony Stark / Iron Man alongside Gwyneth Paltrow, Don Cheadle, Guy Pearce, Rebecca Hall, Stéphanie
Szostak, James Badge Dale, William Sadler, Miguel Ferrer, Jon Favreau, and Ben Kingsley.

14
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
In the film, Stark grapples with the consequences of the events of The Avengers (2012) during a
national terrorism campaign on the United States led by the mysterious Mandarin.

15
01:09:38,571 --> 01:09:44,571
After the release of Iron Man 2 in May 2010, director Jon
Favreau chose not to direct the third film.

16
01:14:17,142 --> 01:14:23,142
Black was hired to write and direct the sequel in February 2011, working with Pearce to make the script more
character-centric, focus on thriller elements, and use concepts from Warren Ellis's "Extremis" comic book story arc.

17
01:18:55,714 --> 01:19:01,714
The film's supporting cast, including Kingsley, Pearce, and Hall,
were brought on throughout April and May 2012.

18
01:23:34,285 --> 01:23:40,285
Filming took place from May 23 to December 17, 2012, primarily at
EUE/Screen Gems Studios in Wilmington, North Carolina.

19
01:28:12,857 --> 01:28:18,857
Additional filming took place around North Carolina as well as in Florida, Los Angeles, and China;
an extended version of the film specifically for Chinese audiences was created.

20
01:32:51,428 --> 01:32:57,428
Seventeen companies provided the film's visual effects.

21
01:37:30,000 --> 01:37:36,000
Iron Man 3 premiered at the Grand Rex in Paris on April 14, 2013, and was released in
the United States on May 3, as the first film in Phase Two of the MCU.

22
01:42:08,571 --> 01:42:14,571
It received positive reviews from critics, with praise for its action sequences, Black's direction,
and Downey's performance, though there was criticism for the portrayal of the Mandarin.

23
01:46:47,142 --> 01:46:53,142
The film was a box office success, grossing over $1.215 billion worldwide, making it the
second-highest-grossing film of 2013 and the sixteenth film to gross over $1 billion.

24
01:51:25,714 --> 01:51:31,714
It finished its theatrical run as the fifth-highest-grossing film of all time,
while its opening weekend was the sixth-highest of all time.

25
01:56:04,285 --> 01:56:10,285
The film received Best Visual Effects nominations at
the Academy Awards and the BAFTA Awards.

26
